From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:18:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: answer the PMU temperature for every panel, quiet
 the TAOC fallback

The firmware asks the AP for the PMU temperature property at boot (callback
D401 "PMUS"/"Temperature") for its panel compensation's initial guess; the
driver answered it only for mini-LED panels, so the OLED K116s logged
"set_PMU_service: failed to read PMU temperature property!" twice. Answer
with the battery temperature as the H17P and v14.7 paths do.

The DCP also reads eleven SMC temperature keys itself for its 2D virtual
temperature model and logs once a second that TAOC is -127.0, the SMC's
no-sample value, and that it uses the 2DVT fallback. TAOC and its siblings
are AOP-sourced sensors the SMC has no sample for until the AOP's sensor
servers run, so route that record to the debug level; another sensor,
value or verdict stays at info.

This is a behaviour change for every panel that is not mini-LED, on
every firmware this template drives: the firmware's PMUS "Temperature"
request used to get "false" there and now gets the battery temperature,
which its panel compensation then takes as the panel's initial
temperature. Mini-LED panels got the temperature before and still do.

Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
[thomas: describe the PMUS reply as a behaviour change]
Signed-off-by: Thomas Glanzmann <thomas@glanzmann.de>
(cherry picked from commit 50db17f86f92b0a68a58f1f28a84a216cdf73552)
[k114s: aurora-silicon/linux pull request 1646 (open, head 907bb7ec5990), commit 1 of 3. Tested upstream on a K116s; not booted on a K114s]
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-syslog-test.c |  9 +++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-syslog.h      | 11 +++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c  | 11 +++++++++--
 3 files changed, 29 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-syslog-test.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-syslog-test.c
index a4442810e8..256343fa38 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-syslog-test.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-syslog-test.c
@@ -18,6 +18,8 @@ static void dcp_syslog_transition_test(struct kunit *test)
 		  "ready_for_run_mode_change: initiating deferred run mode change: 4 -> 1" },
 		{ "UPPipeDCP_H17P.cpp:2014",
 		  "ready_for_run_mode_change: initiating deferred run mode change: 2 -> 4" },
+		{ "itorContext_v4.cpp:1324",
+		  "SMC sensor TAOC is an invalid temp -127.0, using 2DVT fallback values" },
 	};
 	char message[128];
 	int i;
@@ -46,6 +48,13 @@ static void dcp_syslog_unknown_test(struct kunit *test)
 		{ "UPPipeDCP_H17P.cpp:2014", "ready_for_run_mode_change: timeout" },
 		{ "UPPipeDCP_H17P.cpp:2096", "set_run_mode_safe: error -110" },
 		{ "UPPipeDCP_H17P.cpp:2097", "set_run_mode_safe: deferring: 4 -> 1" },
+		/* A different sensor, value or verdict is news. */
+		{ "itorContext_v4.cpp:1324",
+		  "SMC sensor TAOJ is an invalid temp -127.0, using 2DVT fallback values" },
+		{ "itorContext_v4.cpp:1324",
+		  "SMC sensor TAOC is an invalid temp -40.0, using 2DVT fallback values" },
+		{ "itorContext_v4.cpp:1324",
+		  "2DVT thermal sensors valid, using computed virtual temperatures" },
 	};
 	int i;
 
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-syslog.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-syslog.h
index c1bf4f3616..d54897f453 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-syslog.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-syslog.h
@@ -24,6 +24,17 @@ static inline bool dcp_h17p_syslog_is_debug(const char *context, const char *mes
 		       !strcmp(message, "set_run_mode_safe: deferring: 2 -> 4");
 	if (!strcmp(context, "UPPipeDCP_H17P.cpp:2014"))
 		return !strcmp(message, deferred_4_1) || !strcmp(message, deferred_2_4);
+	/*
+	 * The 27.x panel temperature monitor (IOMFBTemperatureMonitorContext_v4)
+	 * reads its sensor keys from the SMC once a second and falls back to the
+	 * default 2D virtual temperature grid while TAOC holds the SMC's -127.0
+	 * "no sample" sentinel (the AOP feeds TAOC/TAOJ/TAOP in macOS; nothing
+	 * does under Linux).  Match the exact record so another sensor or value
+	 * stays visible.
+	 */
+	if (!strcmp(context, "itorContext_v4.cpp:1324"))
+		return !strcmp(message, "SMC sensor TAOC is an invalid temp -127.0, "
+					"using 2DVT fallback values");
 	return false;
 }
 
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c
index c118939c93..3d20d6ca1f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c
@@ -1064,8 +1064,15 @@ dcpep_cb_get_uint_prop(struct apple_dcp *dcp, struct dcp_get_uint_prop_req *req)
 	    .value = 0
 	};
 
-	if (dcp->panel.has_mini_led &&
-	    memcmp(req->obj, "SUMP", sizeof(req->obj)) == 0) { /* "PMUS */
+	/*
+	 * "PMUS"/"Temperature": the battery temperature in 0.1 K.  Every
+	 * firmware with a panel asks for it from TableCompensator::
+	 * set_PMU_service(), mini-LED or not: the OLED firmware (27.x on the
+	 * K116s) uses it as the panel's initial temperature guess and logs
+	 * "failed to read PMU temperature property!" when the reply is
+	 * false.  The H17P table already answers it unconditionally.
+	 */
+	if (memcmp(req->obj, "SUMP", sizeof(req->obj)) == 0) { /* "PMUS */
 	    if (strncmp(req->key, "Temperature", sizeof(req->key)) == 0) {
 		resp.value = dcp_pmu_temperature(dcp->dev);
 		resp.ret = true;
